---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/filter-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Filter study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of filter controls for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="filter-study">
    <div class="shell filter-study-intro">
      <a class="filter-study-back" href="/prototypes/card-study/">← Card study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should browsing feel?</h1>
      <p class="filter-study-lede">Three filter treatments for the transformations page. The controls should help people scan without making the page feel like a dashboard.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell filter-study-grid">
      <article class="filter-option"><p class="filter-option-name"><span>A</span> Underlined choices</p><div class="filter-demo filter-demo--underline"><p>Town</p><div><button class="is-active">All towns</button><button>Dundrum</button><button>Newcastle</button></div></div><p>Lightest visual weight. The active choice is anchored by the same yellow rule as secondary links.</p></article>
      <article class="filter-option"><p class="filter-option-name"><span>B</span> Solid active state</p><div class="filter-demo filter-demo--solid"><p>Town</p><div><button class="is-active">All towns</button><button>Dundrum</button><button>Newcastle</button></div></div><p>Most obvious and easiest to scan. The selected state uses blue; inactive choices stay plain.</p></article>
      <article class="filter-option"><p class="filter-option-name"><span>C</span> Bordered set</p><div class="filter-demo filter-demo--bordered"><p>Town</p><div><button class="is-active">All towns</button><button>Dundrum</button><button>Newcastle</button></div></div><p>A contained control group gives the filters more presence without using rounded pills.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
